  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Information Technology obligated $81.2M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. General Dynamics Information Technology won 17 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.8M. General Dynamics Information Technology saw obligations down 98.3% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years. Department-level concentration is high: the Department of Commerce accounted for $60.5M of FY2027 obligations and the Department of Transportation accounted for $19.3M. Market-level concentration mirrors that split: Other Computer Related Services totaled $60.5M and Computer Systems Design Services totaled $20.5M. Fiscal history shows prior-year full totals of $4.1B in FY22, $4.3B in FY23, $4.8B in FY24, $4.6B in FY25, and $4.9B in FY26, showing FY2027 to date is a partial total for the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are FY2027 obligations by agency and market?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce accounts for the largest share of FY2027 obligations at $60.5M, followed by the Department of Transportation at $19.3M. Other buying agencies with recorded obligations are the General Services Administration at $1.2M and the Environmental Protection Agency at $234K, while several agencies show $0 in obligations. Other Computer Related Services is the largest market at $60.5M and Computer Systems Design Services is next at $20.5M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027-to-date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $81.2M, a partial tally for the current fiscal year. Prior full fiscal years show much larger totals: $4.1B in FY22, $4.3B in FY23, $4.8B in FY24, $4.6B in FY25, and $4.9B in FY26, and FY2027 obligations are down 98.3% year over year."
      }
    ]
  },
